ype\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Named missing owned requirements, contradictions, access/budget limits and highest-impact resolving check.\"},\"stopReason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"Actual sufficient-support, diminishing-return, access, budget or blocked-conclusion reason. Budget stops are not evidence saturation.\"}}}}","status":"completed","runner":"pi","kernel":"typescript","transport":"process","cwd":"/home/balauru/.pi-profiles/fabric/.worktrees/research-skill-rework","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-terra","thinking":"high","startedAt":1788761220622,"updatedAt":1788761358680,"turns":7,"toolCalls":6,"text":"{\"assignment\":\"backups\",\"discovered\":[\"extensions.web_search\",\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"extensions.get_search_content\"],\"calls\":[{\"ref\":\"extensions.web_search\",\"args\":{\"queries\":[\"site:sqlite.org backup API WAL online backup concurrent writes official documentation\",\"site:postgresql.org docs current pg_basebackup online backup WAL recovery official documentation\",\"site:postgresql.org docs current continuous archiving backup recovery pg_basebackup WAL required\"],\"numResults\":5,\"includeContent\":false,\"workflow\":\"none\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"3/3 queries successful; 15 total results.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqu9m7ehjl7oo\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"args\":{\"urls\":[\"https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html\",\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/continuous-archiving.html\"],\"mode\":\"readable\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"4/4 official URLs fetched; 124513 total extracted characters.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqu9r29s2o608\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqu9r29s2o608\",\"urlIndex\":0,\"findText\":[\"The online backup API allows\",\"The source database is read-locked\",\"SQLite holds a write transaction open on the destination database\"],\"findMode\":\"case-insensitive\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"1 matching passage returned; 2 requested phrases had no match.\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqu9r29s2o608\",\"urlIndex\":2,\"offset\":0,\"limit\":30000},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Full 27980-character pg_basebackup document retrieved.\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqu9r29s2o608\",\"urlIndex\":3,\"findText\":[\"a continuous sequence of archived WAL files\",\"starting with the file immediately following the one\",\"base backup is not sufficient\",\"restore_command\",\"recovery.signal\",\"test the recovery procedure\"],\"findMode\":\"case-insensitive\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Matches returned for continuous WAL, restore_command, and recovery.signal; 3 requested phrases had no match.\"}],\"rows\":[{\"id\":\"b1\",\"slot\":\"backup\",\"finding\":\"SQLite documents its Online Backup API as incremental copying in which the source is locked only during actual reads, rather than for the full copy.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html\",\"title\":\"SQLite Backup API\",\"passage\":\"The online backup API allows the contents of one database to be copied into another database file, replacing any original contents of the target database. The copy operation may be done incrementally, in which case the source database does not need to be locked for the duration of the copy, only for the brief periods of time when it is actually being read from.\",\"locator\":\"Online Backup API introduction\",\"origin\":\"SQLite Documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\"}],\"method\":\"Current SQLite documentation URL retrieved. This supports API-level online-copy locking behavior, not a measured backup duration, throughput, or end-to-end restore reliability.\",\"comparability\":\"Not directly comparable to PostgreSQL physical-backup requirements or performance; no matched workload measurement was retrieved.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the stated API locking behavior because it is an exact primary-documentation passage.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"b2\",\"slot\":\"backup\",\"finding\":\"PostgreSQL documents pg_basebackup as an online physical cluster backup; a standalone result requires WAL inclusion, while continuous-archive recovery requires uninterrupted archived WAL reaching back to the backup start.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html\",\"title\":\"pg_basebackup\",\"passage\":\"pg_basebackup is used to take a base backup of a running PostgreSQL database cluster. The backup is taken without affecting other clients of the database, and can be used both for point-in-time recovery\",\"locator\":\"Description\",\"origin\":\"PostgreSQL Global Development Group documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html\",\"title\":\"pg_basebackup\",\"passage\":\"Includes the required WAL (write-ahead log) files in the backup. This will include all write-ahead logs generated during the backup. Unless the method none is specified, it is possible to start a postmaster in the target directory without the need to consult the WAL archive, thus making the output a completely standalone backup.\",\"locator\":\"--wal-method\",\"origin\":\"PostgreSQL Global Development Group documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/continuous-archiving.html\",\"title\":\"25.3. Continuous Archiving and Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR)\",\"passage\":\"To recover successfully using continuous archiving (also called “online backup” by many database vendors), you need a continuous sequence of archived WAL files that extends back at least as far as the start time of your backup. So to get started, you should set up and test your procedure for archiving WAL files before you take your first base backup.\",\"locator\":\"25.3 introduction\",\"origin\":\"PostgreSQL Global Development Group documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\"}],\"method\":\"Current PostgreSQL documentation URL retrieved. Applies to complete-cluster pg_basebackup and continuous-archive recovery, subject to the selected WAL method and recovery configuration.\",\"comparability\":\"SQLite evidence concerns its backup API's source-lock intervals. PostgreSQL evidence concerns physical cluster backup plus WAL retention/recovery; neither source supplies a comparable workload result.\",\"confidence\":\"High for documented pg_basebackup and WAL prerequisites because exact primary passages were retrieved.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"r1\",\"slot\":\"operational-risk\",\"finding\":\"SQLite warns that an operating-system or power failure while copying a database file can leave the backup database corrupted after recovery.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html\",\"title\":\"SQLite Backup API\",\"passage\":\"If a power failure or operating system failure occurs while copying the database file the backup database may be corrupted following system recovery.\",\"locator\":\"Online Backup API introduction\",\"origin\":\"SQLite Documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\"}],\"method\":\"Applies to copying a database file during a failure. It does not establish the failure behavior of every Backup API implementation or backup destination.\",\"comparability\":\"No corresponding fault-injection or restore test was retrieved for either system.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the narrowly worded warning; it is direct SQLite documentation.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"r2\",\"slot\":\"operational-risk\",\"finding\":\"For PostgreSQL pg_basebackup with WAL method fetch, required WAL must remain available until collection finishes; recycled WAL makes the 